{"run_id": "20260815T221206-hepkg-48559", "qid": "gen-concept-c7343da8", "repeat": 1, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "021bd22315cb", "git_sha": "c209974-dirty", "question": "Count the analyses that used the sample Z' signal MC samples (m_Z' = 125-350 GeV, delta_bs = 0.04/0.5/1.0).", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 37 analyses that used the sample Z' signal MC samples (m_Z' = 125-350 GeV, delta_bs = 0.04/0.5/1.0).\n\nThis count is based on the number of distinct papers that have at least one result using this sample. Each paper may have multiple results, leading to a total of 73 facts and 73 assertions in the graph.\n\nTo provide more context, here are some of the specific samples that were found:\n\n- **Z' signal MC samples (m_Z' = 125-350 GeV, delta_bs = 0.04/0.5/1.0)**\n- **W and Z boson signal MC samples (W->l nu, Z->l+l-) at 5.02 and 13 TeV**\n- **Leptoquark signal MC samples**\n- **$t\\bar{t}Z$ signal MC sample**\n- **Z→νν MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)**\n- **Z/γ*→ll MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)**\n- **Sherpa 2.2.1 (13 TeV) / 2.2.5 (5.02 TeV) alternative W/Z signal MC sample (MEPS@NLO)**\n- **Higgs boson signal MC sample (all production modes), MadGraph5_aMC@NLO NLO QCD, m_H=120/125/130 GeV**\n- **SUSY (top squark) signal MC samples**\n- **Signal MC sample: $pp\\rightarrow Z^{\\prime}\\rightarrow s\\chi\\chi\\rightarrow b\\bar{b}\\chi\\chi$ (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO+Pythia8)**\n\nThese samples were used across various analyses, contributing to the overall understanding of the physics processes involved.\n\nIf you need more detailed information about specific papers or results, please let me know.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2107.12553", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.0